w0vncserver: start the PipeWire stream at the size the portal reports

PipeWireStream offers the video size as a range with 1280x720 as the
default. A fixed-size output ignores the default, but KWin resizes a
virtual output to the consumer's default, so the headless kiosk session
dropped to 1280x720 as soon as a VNC client connected. The portal's Start
response carries each stream's size; use it as the default and keep
1280x720 only when the portal doesn't report one.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/TigerVNC/tigervnc/issues/2188

